  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Ifosfamide is an alkylating anticancer drug used to treat various cancers, including sarcomas, lymphomas, and cancers of the breast, ovary, stomach, pancreas, and testis. It is an approved medicine and is included on the WHO list of essential medicines, so it is used widely in cancer care.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q418560&quot;>Wikidata Q418560</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>ifosfamide</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01AA06</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01181&quot;>DB01181</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/3690&quot;>3690</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:5864&quot;>5864</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q418560&quot;>Q418560</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C7H15Cl2N2O2P</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>261.083 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
